{:clarification/id :s2b-fence-witness-clarification-v1
 :scope "Design clarification for F1 and its F3 interaction only, based on immutable edf609c1c96da7a1109bee1e02d3f86874dda7ca objects and the existing review. Not review or approval of a candidate fix."
 :answer "Yes: a closed, bounded, independently replayable synthetic witness can satisfy F1 if every accepted state and emitted intent is exactly reachable under the actual protocol from its validated start configuration. It need not and cannot authenticate a caller-owned history. A fabricated complete valid trace is a valid simulation, never proof that external events happened."
 :correction "F1's phrase 'whose admission cannot be fabricated by raw inputs' must not be read as requiring cryptographic provenance or secret state. The actual requirement is rejection of an internally unreachable state, such as the reviewed pending record with no represented fences."
 :recommended-representation
 {:shape "A closed versioned value containing a validated initial synthetic config and a vector of closed meaningful input commands, each without caller-supplied state. Bound vector length at 256 and enforce all existing byte, node, depth, event and numeric limits. Derive the terminal state and intents; if a state is also supplied, require exact equality across all security-relevant fields, including history, head, pending, counters, time, phase and lease. Never accept supplied intermediate state as an axiom."
  :semantic-core "Replay from start using one pure collector transition function and explicit transition results; reject invalid commands rather than interpreting a refusal as progress. Derive issuance of intents, and require each subsequent reply to correspond to the correct outstanding intent and phase. Reuse frozen desktop validation/replay at event boundaries; do not create a second desktop reducer, ledger authority or private owner adapter."
  :ignored-churn "A compact terminal count and monotonic time may summarize only commands proven semantically inert in the phase where they occurred; a count is not evidence that a loss, timeout, attempt or other state-changing command did not occur. Account exactly for budget consumption and final time, or include those commands. Replay must reject a summary that changes a transition, hides exhaustion, reorders a loss or makes the terminal state unreachable. No implied real-world completeness."
  :alternative "A cut certificate may replace a full command trace only if it composes a complete reachable chain from the initial config through all earlier accepted events, pending resolutions, gaps, losses, attempts and current cut, plus exact terminal state and counters. ACK/pre/snapshot/post alone is insufficient: it cannot establish the predecessor head, active gap, pending identity, intervening loss, or prior accepted history. This certificate is still caller-authored simulation, not a signature or owner proof."
  :bounds "Fail closed if the encoded witness exceeds any existing frame/owned-data limit; do not truncate, discard state-changing inputs or silently weaken the 256 cap. If existing bounds cannot encode a required legal scenario, expose the incompatibility for a separately reviewed boundary decision."}
 :acceptance-oracles
 [{:id :unreachable-pending :expect "Starting from the reviewed begun config, add baseline pending/H0/H1 and a matching accepted result without its successful subscription and exact pre/snapshot/post schedule: reject, no fixture freshness and no admission intent. Mutating phase, attempt, cut, head, history or lease alone must also fail equality with the derived state."}
  {:id :valid-simulation :expect "A complete valid caller-authored subscribe-ACK, matching non-first pre tick, snapshot, matching non-first post tick and exact synthetic acceptance derives the expected fixture pending and then fresh state. The result remains :authority :none; do not claim authenticity, unobserved event absence or operational freshness."}
  {:id :fences-and-loss :expect "Omit/reorder either tick, use tick reply or first tick, reuse/wrong nonce, wrong generation, stale deadline, or insert a represented stream change between fences: no accepted cut. Insert loss after pending then exact late acceptance: account exact admitted head but revoke lease and require the lawful gap. Same for stale gap and reconciliation, without duplicate or competing events."}
  {:id :gaps-and-links :expect "Reject reconciliation without an admitted active gap or with wrong direct cause, revision, predecessor, event bytes or incarnation under frozen replay; reject fabricated gap pending without reachable admitted prior history and loss. Exact unchanged-head rejection permits only the lawful bounded retry; unknown or conflicting proof preserves the same pending identity."}
  {:id :budgets-and-expiry :expect "At most three subscription attempts including failures; no new work at or beyond the deadline; freshness is false exactly at lease expiry. Check monotonic time, generation and attempt exhaustion and witness/state equality. A fabricated complete valid trace is accepted only as fixture simulation."}
  {:id :resolution-after-cap :expect "Reach pending through a real synthetic schedule; consume the remaining ordinary step budget with valid inert inputs or a validated equivalent summary. At the cap ordinary scheduling emits no competing admission. A separately initiated bounded exact head-resolution can still account for the same pending event and head after cap or deadline; matching acceptance/rejection follows the V3 branch, never restores an old lease or resets normal attempts/deadline. Wrong, incomplete or conflicting evidence remains uncertain and emits no competing admission. Test stale baseline, gap and reconciliation, plus unchanged-head rejection and repeated resolution idempotence."}]
 :work-control {:target "Single witness validation is linear in command count plus bounded event validation/replay costs, with explicit finite input bounds; avoid recursively invoking public state validation or revalidating every trace prefix from scratch. Validate event history at most once per necessary event boundary, using the existing frozen law."
                :qualification "Revalidating a growing caller-supplied trace on every separate public request can still be quadratic across a sequence; do not promise aggregate linearity without a justified trusted cache or batching. No cache may become semantic authority or bypass validation."
                :tests "Instrument transition and frozen-replay call counts; compare one-shot short and near-cap witnesses in BB and NBB and run a practical bounded-time cap regression. Include exactly-at-cap and +1, large allowed events, repeated ignored churn, and fail-closed oversized witnesses. Do not rely solely on wall-clock or cubic repeated nested replay."
                :resolution-rate "A stateless API can bound work and resolution input per invocation, but cannot enforce a global limit on repeated external calls without separate state or authority; do not claim otherwise."}
 :limits [:no-native-i3 :no-real-owner-proof :no-private-append :no-dependency-install :no-source-edit :no-git-write :no-board-or-ledger :no-nested-agents :no-candidate-inspection]
 :next "Implement and test within the existing permit; request a new exact-head review before treating F1 or F3 as settled."}
